  "answer": "The archive holds two XBRL concepts for AAPL's revenue metric: us-gaap:SalesRevenueNet and us-gaap:Revenues. Both are mapped to the ST-EVA 'revenue' metric with mapping_type PARTIAL (not EXACT), and both have series_continues: false. The semantic metadata records CONCEPT_MAPPING_BREAK series breaks for each concept: us-gaap:SalesRevenueNet effective 2007-09-29 to 2018-06-30, and us-gaap:Revenues effective 2016-09-24 to 2018-09-29. Because the mappings are partial, the series do not continue across the concept boundary, and explicit concept-mapping breaks are recorded, the two concept series cannot be read as one continuous comparable series.",
  "evidence_refs": ["obsarch_ddb4af888ab3c6be910c0f9e", "obsarch_aea878acdf7f37c0b6d160b6"],
  "derived_refs": [],
  "uncertainties": ["The exact date when AAPL switched from reporting us-gaap:SalesRevenueNet to us-gaap:Revenues in its primary filings is not explicitly stated; the mapping windows overlap from 2016-09-24 to 2018-06-30."]
